message: "If you use this repository, please cite it as below and cite the upstream codes listed in README.md."
title: "Atmospheric Memory under Repeated Electron-Beam Heating: When Does the Independent-Pulse Approximation Fail?"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Martínez Sibaja"
    given-names: "Carlos Alberto"
    alias: "carlmarx17"
repository-code: "https://github.com/carlmarx17/GrazTrabajo"
license: MIT
abstract: "Research framework that measures, with paired radiation-hydrodynamic simulation branches, when treating each electron pulse as if it struck the relaxed atmosphere misrepresents the response to a later pulse by more than numerical, beam and observational uncertainties, with STIX-based observational extensions."
keywords:
  - solar flares
  - hard X-rays
  - STIX
  - radiation hydrodynamics
  - electron beams
  - atmospheric memory
  - Fokker–Planck transport
